oggle buttons, and option buttons on a form, report, or data access page. You use an option group to present alternatives from which the user can select a single option.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145640">option group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402272">اختیار گروپ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11558_181384_1962511"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A dialog box that displays information about an object in the interface.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="181384">properties page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1962511">خواص صفحہ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11563_109159_409938"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data structure that contains security information associated with a protected object. Security descriptors include information about who owns the object, who can access it and in what way, and what types of access are audited.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109159">security descriptor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="409938">حفاظتی تفصیل</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11564_235069_402606"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that allows for ease of creating a new or expanding an existing wireless network. This setup can be done automatically using a USB flash driver or manually through a Wireless Network Setup wizard.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235069">Windows Connect Now</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402606">۔Windows اب جوڑیں</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11567_216558_402497"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To arrange to receive a product or use a service regularly.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="216558">subscribe</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402497">رکن بنیں</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11568_397198_409927"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mailbox server that is installed in a Windows failover cluster. A clustered mailbox server is used in both cluster continuous replication (CCR) and single copy cluster (SCC) configurations. A clustered mailbox server was called an Exchange Virtual Server in previous versions of Exchange Server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397198">clustered mailbox server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="409927">کلسٹر والا میل باکس سرور</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11576_358360_361328"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of components and services that enable voice, fax, and email messages to be stored in a user's single mailbox. Users can also access their Microsoft Exchange Server 2007 mailbox from a telephone or a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358360">Unified Messaging server role</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="361328">پیغام بھیجنے کے سرور کی مجموعی ذمہ داریاں</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11584_308343_402898"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphic ad that is the full height of a page and normally 120 pixels wide.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="308343">skyscraper</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><n