ip type="definition">A graphical user interface control that is equipped with a small bar which slides along a visible line and is used to set a value along a range with a minimum and maximum.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="641191">slider control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402046">سلائیڈر</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14511_2148_401276"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To reduce a window to a button on the taskbar by clicking the Minimize button (leftmost button on the right side of the title bar) or by pressing ALT+SPACEBAR and then pressing N.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2148">minimize</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401276">چھوٹا کریں</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14523_360144_403241"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A window that displays the SQL statement for the current query or that is used to create an SQL-specific query (union, pass-through, or data definition). When you create a query in Design view, Access constructs the SQL equivalent in SQL view.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="360144">SQL view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="403241">۔SQL منظر</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14526_360146_403243"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query that asks a question about the data stored in your tables and returns a result set in the form of a datasheet, without changing the data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="360146">select query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="403243">طلب منتخب کریں</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14528_276550_1994911"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A single location in Windows where you can adjust mobile PC settings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="276550">Windows Mobility Center</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1994911">Windows حرکت پذیری مرکز</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14534_21247_2247481"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that contains encoded information that is interpreted according to the application that created it. In general, a binary file can be edited only by the application in which it was created.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21247">binary file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2247481">ثنائی فائل</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14540_373951_1433949"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An interactive technology in Microsoft Excel or Access that can show dynamic views of the same data from a list or a database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="373951">Microsoft PivotTable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1433949">PivotTable</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14540_373952_1433949"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An interactive technology in Microsoft Excel or Access that can show dynamic views of the same data from a list or a database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="373952">PivotTable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1433949">PivotTable</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14543_231973_402521"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft Office Web Component that allows you to create a structure similar to an Excel PivotTable report. Users can view the PivotTable list in a Web browser and change its layout in a manner similar to an Excel PivotTable report.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231973">PivotTable list</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402521">۔PivotTable فہرست</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14562_318120_402979"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The button on your pointing device that you use to display shortcut menus or other program-specific features.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318120">right mouse button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402979">دایاں ماؤس بٹن</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14574_123914_1217533"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Confidence in the reliability of an entity or service and the information that it provides.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="123914">trust</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1217533">اعتماد</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14579_60118_401723"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user interface control that facilitates modification of an object's appearance, position, or behavior.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="60118">handle</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401723">ہینڈل</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14584_358355_361308"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that ensures that a mobile device automatically retrieves new email from the Microsoft Exchange server. Direct Push uses a longstanding HTTPS connection that is maintained by the mobile device to push new email messages, Calendar, Contacts, and Tasks notifications from the server to the device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358355">Direct Push</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="361308">براہ راست فراہمی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14585_329892_403119"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A change to an account to correct or update the balance.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="329892">adjustment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="403119">تسویہ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14606_211370_402460"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The date by which some task or action should be completed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="211370">due date</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402460">واجب تاریخ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14609_183539_2463862"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An artificial intelligence program that performs a task on a network as an agent for a user or another program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="183539">bot</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2463862">بوٹ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14609_183540_2463862"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An artificial intelligence program that performs a task on a network as an agent for a user or another program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="183540">robot</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2463862">بوٹ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14610_25574_401443"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphic element that appears similar to a physical button or keyboard key in the UI. A button is "pressed" by clicking on it with a mouse, by hitting ENTER or RETURN on the keyboard (if the button has the focus) or tapping by a finger.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="25574">button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401443">بٹن</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14611_123792_1217534"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An automated tool that helps find and fix specific problems on your computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="123792">troubleshooter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1217534">ازالہ کار</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14612_73965_401819"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The key on the keyboard that is labeled with a left arrow.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73965">left arrow</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401819">بایاں تیر</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14617_93343_401962"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of industry-standard framing and authentication protocols that are included with Windows to ensure interoperability with other remote access software. PPP negotiates configuration parameters for multiple layers of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model. The Internet standard for serial communications, PPP defines how data packets are exchanged with other Internet-based systems using a modem connection. PPP is documented in RFC 1661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93343">Point-to-Point Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401962">نکتہ بہ نکتہ پروٹوکول</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14617_93343_401963"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of industry-standard framing and authentication protocols that are included with Windows to ensure interoperability with other remote access software. PPP negotiates configuration parameters for multiple layers of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model. The Internet standard for serial communications, PPP defines how data packets are exchanged with other Internet-based systems using a modem connection. PPP is documented in RFC 1661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93343">Point-to-Point Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401963">PPP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14617_93344_401962"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of industry-standard framing and authentication protocols that are included with Windows to ensure interoperability with other remote access software. PPP negotiates configuration parameters for multiple layers of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model. The Internet standard for serial communications, PPP defines how data packets are exchanged with other Internet-based systems using a modem connection. PPP is documented in RFC 1661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93344">PPP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401962">نکتہ بہ نکتہ پروٹوکول</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14617_93344_401963"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of industry-standard framing and authentication protocols that are included with Windows to ensure interoperability with other remote access software. PPP negotiates configuration parameters for multiple layers of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model. The Internet standard for serial communications, PPP defines how data packets are exchanged with other Internet-based systems using a modem connection. PPP is documented in RFC 1661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93344">PPP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401963">PPP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14619_136078_1217535"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An email security feature used to request confirmation that a message was received unaltered and information about who opened the message and when it was opened. This verification information is returned as a message to your Inbox.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136078">S/MIME receipt</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1217535">S/MIME رسید</