 that allows users to switch back to recently used apps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1755689">app switching</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1758261">ایپ سوئچنگ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33088_1755690_1758262"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The state that enables a PC to turn on instantly and have tiles and other services update even when the screen is off.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1755690">connected standby</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1758262">متصل پیش تیار</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33089_1755691_1758264"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of Windows and device settings that users can change grouped into one location.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1755691">PC settings</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1758264">PC  سیٹنگیں</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3309_375734_380534"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Functionality in Exchange Server 2007 that helps the messaging administrator diagnose spam-related problems by applying diagnostic metadata, or "stamps," such as sender-specific information, puzzle validation results, and content filtering results, to messages as they pass through the anti-spam features that filter inbound messages from the Internet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="375734">anti-spam stamping</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="380534">اسپام مخالف اسٹامپ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33091_1755693_1758267"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tablet hardware button with the Windows logo on it that's similar to the Windows key on a keyboard. Pressing the Power and Windows buttons simultaneously is the equivalent of pressing Ctrl+Alt+Del.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1755693">Windows button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1758267">Windows بٹن</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33092_1755782_1760872"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The spreading of malicious content through online advertising.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1755782">malvertising</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1760872">مضر اشتہار بازی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33092_1755783_1760872"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The spreading of malicious content through online advertising.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1755783">malicious advertising</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1760872">مضر اشتہار بازی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33093_1755827_1778366"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A rating of how safe an app is determined to be by SmartScreen, according to age, presence of digital certificate, and other criteria.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1755827">SmartScreen Application Reputation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778366">SmartScreen ایپلیکیشن ساکھ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><ter