feature that enables customers to provide and control their own encryption keys used to encrypt their Microsoft data at rest.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3043787">Microsoft Purview Customer Key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3044121">Microsoft Purview کسٹمر کلید</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46353_2612185_2612502"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The consumer-friendly name for virtualization-based security (VBS). The VBS service in Windows 10 uses hardware virtualization features to create and isolate a secure region of memory from the normal operating system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612185">Core isolation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612502">بنیادی حد سازی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46354_2612186_2612503"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of open tabs, including applications, files, pages, or websites, which can be saved together and re-opened together when you want to continue with that set of tabs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612186">set</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612503">مجموعہ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46375_2612854_2923122"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A date when Microsoft will no longer provide updates to a feature release of a product, such that a customer needs to upgrade to a new feature release to continue receiving support from Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612854">end of service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2923122">سروس کا اختتام</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46375_2878237_2923122"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A date when Microsoft will no longer provide updates to a feature release of a product, such that a customer needs to upgrade to a new feature release to continue receiving support from Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2878237">EOL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2923122">سروس کا اختتام</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46381_3128246_3128731"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature for Windows commercial customers that helps mitigate security threats by restricting the applications that users are allowed to run and the code that runs in the System Core (kernel).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128246">App Control for Business</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128731">ایپ کنٹرول</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46381_3128246_3128732"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature for Windows commercial customers that helps mitigate security threats by restricting the applications that users are allowed to run and the code that runs in the System Core (kernel).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128246">App Control for Business</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128732">ایپ کنٹرول برائے کاروبار</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46381_3128314_3128731"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature for Windows commercial customers that helps mitigate security threats by restricting the applications that users are allowed to run and the code that runs in the System Core (kernel).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128314">App Control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128731">ایپ کنٹرول</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46381_3128314_3128732"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature for Windows commercial customers that helps mitigate security threats by restricting the applications that users are allowed to run and the code that runs in the System Core (kernel).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128314">App Control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128732">ایپ کنٹرول برائے کاروبار</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4639_108282_402018"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To move a document or other data in a window in order to view a particular portion of the document. Scrolling may be controlled by the mouse, arrow keys, or other keys on the keyboard, eventually with one or more fingers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="108282">scroll</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402018">سکرول کریں</term><termNote type="geographicalUs