teristic of text, such as font, size, style, color, or effect such as subscript or superscript.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149177">text attributes</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1934267">متن اوصاف</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="803_44794_401600"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The work area on a computer screen that simulates the top of an actual desk. The desktop contains the Recycle Bin and other icons (shortcuts to programs, files, folders, and various types of documents such as letters, reports, or pictures) that you can arrange on the electronic desktop just as you would arrange real objects on top of a desk.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44794">desktop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="401600">ڈیسک ٹاپ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8030_37385_2297798"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To join sequentially (for example, to combine the two strings "hello" and "there" into the single string "hello there").</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="37385">concatenate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2297798">concatenate</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8036_116444_402065"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A horizontal window at the bottom of a parent window in which an application can display various kinds of status information. The status bar can be divided into parts to display more than one type of information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116444">status bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402065">حالت بار</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8040_149410_402306"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query that uses the UNION operator to combine the results of two or more select queries.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149410">union query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="402306">مجموعی طلب</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8043_94462_1217466"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In word processors and other applications, the feature that formats a document for printing but displays it on the video monitor rather than sending it directly to the printer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="94462">preview</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1217466">پیش منظر</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8051_109321_1962643"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Windows-based computers, an account (such as a user, security group, device, or computer) that can be granted or denied access to resources.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109321">security principal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1962643">اصول</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8051_109321_409942"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Windows-based computers, an account (such as a user, security group, device, or computer) that can be granted or denied access to resources.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109321">security principal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ur"><ntig><termGrp><term id="409942">حفاظتی اصول</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">PAK</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Nou